\par ANSWER: The responsibility for providing health care in the Federation of BiH is divided between the Federation and its Cantons. The system is criticized for being convoluted and inefficient. The quality of treatment a patient receives can vary significan
tly, depending on his or her Canton of residence. In contrast, the health care system in Republika Srpska is both easier to navigate and better at providing equal treatment to all its subjects.
\par Unemployed persons who have not registered their status are not
 covered by the health care system of the Federation of BiH. The time frame for registering as unemployed is very narrow; as such, many of the recently unemployed fall out of the health care system. Additionally, a person can lose coverage if his or her e
mployer fails to pay the appropriate health care payments. The dependents of an uncovered person are also without coverage.
